We have, $A=\left[\begin{array}{cc}1 & -3 \\ 2 & k\end{array}\right]$
Now, $\quad A=\left[\begin{array}{cc}1 & -3 \\ 2 & k\end{array}\right]\left[\begin{array}{cc}1 & -3 \\ 2 & k\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1-6 & -3-3 k \\
2+2 k & -6+k^{2}
\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-5 & -3-3 k \\
2+2 k & k^{2}-6
\end{array}\right]$
Now, $A^{2}-4 A+10 I=A\begin{aligned} \Rightarrow\left[\begin{array}{cc}-5 & -3-3 k \\ 2+2 k & k^{2}-6\end{array}\right]-4\left[\begin{array}{cc}1 & -3 \\ 2 & k\end{array}\right] \\ &+10\left[\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}1 & -3 \\ 2 & k\end{array}\right] \end{aligned}\begin{aligned}
&\Rightarrow\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-5-4+10 & -3-3 k+12+0 \\
2+2 k-8+0 & k^{2}-6-4 k+10
\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 & -3 \\
2 & k
\end{array}\right] \\
&\Rightarrow\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-1 & -3 k+9 \\
2 k-6 & k^{2}-4 k+4
\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 & -3 \\
2 & k
\end{array}\right]
\end{aligned}$
On comparing both sides, we get
$k^{2}-4 k+4=k\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow & k^{2}-5 k+4=0 \\ \Rightarrow & k^{2}-4 k-k+4=0 \\ \Rightarrow & k(k-4)-1(k-4)=0 \\ \Rightarrow & (k-4)(k-1)=0 \\ \Rightarrow & k=4,1\end{array}$

We have, $A=\left[\begin{array}{lll}1 & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\ 1 & 3 & 4\end{array}\right], B=\left[\begin{array}{c}7 \\ 16 \\ 22\end{array}\right]$
X=\left[\begin{array}{l}
x \\
y \\
z
\end{array}\right]

Now, $A X=B$
\begin{aligned}
&x+y+z=7 \quad \text{...(i)} \\
&x+2 y+3 z=16 \quad \text{...(ii)} \\
&x+3 y+4 z=22 \quad \text{...(iii)}
\end{aligned}

Subtracting Eq. (i) from Eq. (ii), we get

y+2 z=9 \quad \text{...(iv)}

Subtracting Eq. (iii) from Eq. (ii), we get

y+z=6 \quad \text{...(v)}

Subtracting Eq. (v) from Eq. (iv), we get 
$z=3$
